# placement table (SPEC §11.3): policy | situation -> action
exact         | equal bytes                     -> noop
exact         | F starts with C (superset)      -> conflict
exact         | C starts with F (stale prefix)  -> conflict
exact         | linked classic fragment         -> conflict
exact         | unrelated                       -> conflict
jsonl-append  | equal bytes                     -> noop
jsonl-append  | F starts with C (superset)      -> keep-existing
jsonl-append  | C starts with F (stale prefix)  -> replace
jsonl-append  | linked classic fragment         -> merge
jsonl-append  | unrelated                       -> conflict
line-union    | equal bytes                     -> noop
line-union    | F starts with C (superset)      -> line-union
line-union    | C starts with F (stale prefix)  -> line-union
line-union    | linked classic fragment         -> line-union
line-union    | unrelated                       -> line-union
sqlite-group  | equal bytes                     -> noop
sqlite-group  | F starts with C (superset)      -> conflict
sqlite-group  | C starts with F (stale prefix)  -> conflict
sqlite-group  | linked classic fragment         -> conflict
sqlite-group  | unrelated                       -> conflict
md            | equal bytes                     -> noop
md            | F starts with C (superset)      -> conflict
md            | C starts with F (stale prefix)  -> conflict
md            | linked classic fragment         -> conflict
md            | unrelated                       -> conflict
(unknown)     | equal bytes                     -> noop
(unknown)     | F starts with C (superset)      -> conflict
(unknown)     | C starts with F (stale prefix)  -> conflict
(unknown)     | linked classic fragment         -> conflict
(unknown)     | unrelated                       -> conflict
